            <ArticleTitle>Tick-borne encephalitis and concomitant infection with Borrelia burgdorferi.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Concomitant tick-borne encephalitis and Borrelia infection in 43 year old farmer living in a village on the border of the Knyszyn Forest was described. Diagnosis was based on anamnesis and objective examination, and was confirmed by serological tests.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
